    "title": "Site audit clock: the site asks GitHub to run the audit's checks on time",
    "why": "handoffs/site-audit.md item 1 (decisions/0145): GitHub skips or delays scheduled runs when busy (the 09:43 browser checks ran at 17:44, then stopped), so Site health, the paths and the audit went stale. A new hourly job (Site audit clock, audit_clock_tick) asks GitHub through repository_dispatch with the existing GITHUB_DOCS_TOKEN: the code checks at 7:00 and 19:00 UTC, the browser checks and paths at 9:00, the search probe at 10:00. Site health in Pulse now says when a check hasn't run in 26 hours, with Run it now; its Run the checks now step is a button too. Staff-only; nothing visitors see, so no FAQ change. Never runs on staging.",
